      en: "Spean Thma is a 12th-century stone bridge built by Jayavarman VII, located east of Angkor Thom. The name means 'Stone Bridge'. It is part of the ancient road network connecting Angkor to the eastern provinces. The bridge is about 30 meters long and 10 meters wide, with multiple corbelled arches. It was constructed using sandstone and laterite, typical of Khmer engineering. Unlike the larger Spean Praptos, Spean Thma spans a smaller stream. The bridge is well-preserved, with some original balustrades intact. It is less visited, offering a serene setting amid the forest.",
